# Every construct, once

Carve swaps the delimiters Markdown got backwards: *strong*, /emphasis/,
_underline_, ~strikethrough~ and =highlight=. Sub and sup are braced-only, so
H{,2,}O and mc{^2^} cannot be mistaken for punctuation. Forced spellings reach
inside a word: my{_path_}name.

Inline: `code`, !`literal code`, $`e^{i\pi}+1=0`, [a link](https://example.com),
![an image](logo.svg), <https://autolink.example>, </#intro>, [ref][],
[@knuth1984], :kbd[Ctrl], :smile:, @mention, #tag, and a footnote[^note].

An inline footnote ^[carried right here] and editorial marks: {+inserted+},
{-deleted-}, {~old~>new~}, {#a reviewer note#}. Typography: -> <- --> <=> ...
and an em dash --- mid-sentence. Escapes hold: \*not strong\*.

